{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your cardiac surgery team doctors. You’re here today for your coronary artery bypass surgery. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little nervous, but okay. I’ve been having more trouble walking without getting short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly why we’re doing this. Your heart isn’t getting enough blood through two major arteries, and this bypass will help improve that. You’ve already had all the tests, and everything looks ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep the whole time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under general anesthesia. The surgery takes a few hours. We’ll use your internal mammary artery and a vein from your leg to create three new pathways around the blocked areas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidneys? I know they’ve been weak since last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring that closely. Your baseline creatinine is 1.5, and we’ll avoid anything that could stress your kidneys. Nephrology is on board if we need them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2115-02-28 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2115-02-28 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just updating you — you’re in the recovery area now. The surgery went well. You’ve had a triple bypass: one artery from your chest and two vein grafts to your heart. You’re on a breathing machine for now, but that’s expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2115-02-28 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just reviewed your chest X-ray. The breathing tube is in a good spot, but we’ll adjust it slightly. Your lungs look clear, which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2115-02-28 21:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m back. Your breathing has gotten a little faster, so we checked another X-ray. There’s mild fluid in the lungs — common after surgery. We’ll watch it closely and adjust your fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2115-02-28 22:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I feel a little tight in my chest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2115-02-28 22:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. Your heart is adjusting after surgery, and we’re giving you just the right amount of fluid. It should improve in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2115-03-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re off the breathing machine now. You were extubated this morning and breathing on your own. How’s your breathing feel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2115-03-01 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still weak, but I can breathe. What’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2115-03-01 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started a beta-blocker and a diuretic to help your heart work efficiently and reduce fluid. We’ll also remove the Swan-Ganz catheter and put in a central line for medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2115-03-01 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray confirms the new central line is in place. Your lungs still have some atelectasis — collapsed areas — but that’s common. We’ll keep encouraging deep breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2115-03-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest tubes were removed this morning. That’s a big step. You’re healing well, and your breathing is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2115-03-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little better. But my legs are swelling a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2115-03-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, some swelling is expected. We’re watching your kidney function closely because your creatinine went up to 3.1. That means your kidneys aren’t filtering as well right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2115-03-02 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? Last time it caused problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2115-03-02 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s acute on chronic kidney injury — we expected this risk. Nephrology is involved, and we’ve paused the diuretic for now. The good news is your urine output is good, and your weight is slowly coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2115-03-03 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Another X-ray shows your heart is a bit enlarged, but no change in fluid. We’re not concerned about tamponade. Your lungs still have some atelectasis, but it’s stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2115-03-04 07:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for pulmonary edema. The latest X-ray shows improvement in lung fluid, which is excellent. Your heart is adjusting well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2115-03-04 18:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The cardiac silhouette is slightly larger, but you’re not showing signs of tamponade. We’ll keep monitoring. If anything changes, we’ll do an echo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2115-03-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling a burning when I pee. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2115-03-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be a urinary tract infection. We’ll test your urine. With the catheter, UTIs can happen after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2115-03-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine test came back — you have Pseudomonas, a type of bacteria. It’s sensitive to ciprofloxacin, so we’re starting that antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2115-03-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2115-03-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not if we treat it. Pseudomonas can be tough, but cipro will work. You should feel better in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2115-03-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been nauseous. Vomited once last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2115-03-06 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray. It was hard to see, but there’s no sign of a blockage. Nausea can happen after surgery, especially with antibiotics. We’ll give something for nausea and keep you hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news — your creatinine is stable at 2.9, and your infection is responding. You’re making real progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go to rehab soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’ll go to extended care rehab. You’re still weak and need help moving, but your wounds are healing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my diabetes? My sugars have been okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose has been under good control. You’ve only needed insulin occasionally. As you eat more, we’ll watch closely. If sugars go above 140 often, we’ll adjust."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on clopidogrel, amlodipine, metoprolol, and rosuvastatin. We’re switching from nebivolol to metoprolol because it’s safer with your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember I’m allergic to aspirin. Is that still an issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but you’re on clopidogrel instead — it’s similar and safe for you. No aspirin. We’ll keep that on your chart clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my legs? They still hurt from the vein harvest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The incisions are healing well — no redness or drainage. You can use tramadol for pain. Keep them clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my chest?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The sternum is healing well. No signs of infection. Wear a supportive bra to reduce pulling. No lifting over 10 pounds for 10 weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t be able to drive?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for about a month. Wait until your follow-up with the surgeon. Safety first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need help at rehab?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll need two people to help you move for now. Your goal is to walk with a cane again. You’ve had a stroke before, so rehab will focus on strength and balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What labs will I need?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Twice weekly blood tests for kidney function — BUN, creatinine, and potassium. The results go straight to nephrology. We’ll follow up with cardiology and surgery too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will my kidney get better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We expect it will improve over time. It’s a combination of your chronic condition and the stress of surgery. Staying hydrated and avoiding certain meds will help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2115-03-07 08:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel more at ease now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day. Your labs are stable, infection is treated, and your heart is doing well. We’re discharging you to rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. Nervous, but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. Remember: shower daily, check your incisions, weigh yourself every morning, and take your temperature at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No creams on the cuts?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct — no lotions or powders. Just mild soap and water. And call us if you see redness, drainage, or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2115-03-08 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You’ve been through a lot, and you’re on the mend. Rehab will help you regain strength. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2115-03-08 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last X-ray before discharge — shows your heart size is stable, no fluid in lungs. Everything looks good for transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2115-03-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go. Just want to keep getting better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2115-03-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will. Keep up the deep breathing, stay active as you can, and follow the rehab team’s guidance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2115-03-08 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2115-03-08 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. We’re proud of your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forgot — what about the heparin shots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll get heparin injections three times a day to prevent clots. The rehab nurses will give them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stool softener?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Docusate twice a day, and polyethylene glycol daily. We don’t want constipation — it can strain your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll follow everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2115-03-08 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re well prepared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2115-03-08 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m a little sad to leave — you all have taken such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2115-03-08 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad we could help. This is just the next step. You’ve had a major surgery, and you’re healing well. We’ll see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2115-03-08 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2115-03-08 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check — incisions clean, breathing good, vitals stable. You’re cleared for transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2115-03-08 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2115-03-08 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call us with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2115-03-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2115-03-08 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep getting stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2115-03-08 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll miss you all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2115-03-08 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll miss you too. But this is a good goodbye — you’re on the road to recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2115-03-08 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so grateful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2115-03-08 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And we’re proud of you. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2115-03-08 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Safe travels to rehab. We’ll be checking in."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2115-02-28 08:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2115-03-08 16:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for elective coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) due to severe two-vessel coronary disease and worsening dyspnea on exertion. She underwent a successful triple bypass using the left internal mammary artery and saphenous vein grafts. Postoperatively, she was managed in the CVICU, extubated on postoperative day 2, and transitioned to the telemetry floor by day 6. She developed acute kidney injury with rising creatinine from 1.5 to 3.1, prompting nephrology consultation and discontinuation of diuretics. A urinary tract infection caused by Pseudomonas aeruginosa was identified and treated with ciprofloxacin. Her wounds healed well, and she was discharged on postoperative day 8 to extended care rehabilitation with plans for close outpatient follow-up, including twice-weekly renal labs. Medications were adjusted for safety, including switching from nebivolol to metoprolol and continuing clopidogrel instead of aspirin due to allergy.",
    "problems": [
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Pulmonary insufficiency following trauma and surgery",
      "Acute kidney failure with lesion of tubular necrosis",
      "Late effects of cerebrovascular disease, hemiplegia affecting unspecified side",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Diabetes with other specified manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage I through stage IV, or unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
